# API Rules

Use REST-style endpoints.

Version all APIs with /api/v1.

Use plural resource names.

Examples:
- POST /api/v1/auth/register
- POST /api/v1/auth/login
- GET /api/v1/services
- POST /api/v1/bookings
- PATCH /api/v1/bookings/{id}/cancel
- POST /api/v1/payments/create-order
- POST /api/v1/payments/webhook

# Handler Rules

Handlers must:
- decode request
- validate input
- call service
- return standard response

Handlers must not:
- query database directly
- contain payment business logic
- contain booking state logic

# Status Codes

Use:
- 200 for success
- 201 for created
- 400 for validation error
- 401 for unauthenticated
- 403 for unauthorized
- 404 for not found
- 409 for conflict
- 500 for internal error